# ---- offsets, flags and ids: value <name> <number> -----------------------------------------
# COPIED framework offsets. mode_mask_busy, clip_layer and surface_playing were exercised by
# the run (in_game went true in a game; the example clip drew full screen). The event and
# node offsets were not exercised. Godzilla's light owner, light set and award screen type are
# its own rules' ids and are LEFT OUT, so lights are off on Jaws. The award screen offsets are
# left out too: with no known Jaws award screen type there is nothing to call them with.
value mode_mask_busy        0x210
value event_next            0x84
value event_flags           0x2
value event_show_flag       0x20
value event_show_id         0x96
value scene_player_scene    0x10
value node_visible_vfn      0xa8
value display_at            0x7c
value surface_playing       2
value clip_layer            0

# ---- shots: shot <mask> <name> - from a one-switch-at-a-time census in the emulator ---------
# Jaws sends 0x1 and the shot bit in ONE dispatch (Godzilla sends two).
shot 0x2               Left slingshot
shot 0x4               Right slingshot
shot 0x8               Left return lane
shot 0x20              Right return lane
shot 0x80              Right pop bumper
# the spinner sends 0x100, 0x400 and 0x800 in one spin
shot 0x100             Spinner
# the upper playfield ship wheel sends 0x1000, 0x2000, 0x4000 and 0x8000 as it turns
shot 0x1000            Ship wheel
shot 0x400000          Chum bucket target
shot 0x4000000         Left ramp enter
# 1.5 s after Left ramp enter when the ramp's made switch did not follow; meaning not measured
shot 0x10000000        Left ramp enter, late
shot 0x8000000         Left ramp
shot 0x20000000        Center ramp
shot 0x40000000        Right ramp
shot 0x80000000        Upper playfield ramp
shot 0x100000000       Target 1
shot 0x200000000       Target 2
shot 0x400000000       Target 3
shot 0x800000000       Bottom right target
shot 0x2000000000      Upper playfield target
shot 0x4000000000      3 bank bottom
shot 0x8000000000      3 bank middle
shot 0x10000000000     3 bank top
# sent with 3 bank top after the bottom and middle were down: probably the bank completed
shot 0x20000000000     3 bank complete
shot 0x400000000000    Mid flipper lane
shot 0x8000000000000   Quickshot top
shot 0x10000000000000  Quickshot middle
shot 0x20000000000000  Quickshot bottom
# no shot from: the three boat hit optos, shark hit, shark fin target (their mechs were not
# moved), and the left loop entrance (0x1 only: a loop needs its exit too)

# ---- callouts by role, scenes by role -------------------------------------------------------------
# cmode_timed's own defaults (0x1b8da8 stores them at +0x84/+0x86/+0x88; its countdown virtual
# 0x1b7c40 plays them): the same roles as Godzilla's 1287/1291/1295. The run was muted: the
# requests ran without a fault, but which sound plays is not heard yet.
# Jaws has no slide-out scene like Godzilla's 32e6ae28. UIScoreFrame loads the score panel
# 9d578751 (the same id as Godzilla's score panel). NOT yet proven as a home for a screen.
scene hud                  9d57875196c613785a1eee010c55223a0f1aa821
# the same scene id as Godzilla's; 635 clips, and video_bank.parse walks it
scene video_bank           60ed7e5036b8ce09d35a3e101ea6fc1380b37d97
scene attract              394c4a037fb26e12f536c42b2677bfed831f5c98

# ---- callouts, heard in the emulator 2026-09-24 (item 163): the runtime's callout / callout_nth
# sites played each id and the game's audio was transcribed: countdown 1386 (clips 1-5 said "ONE", "2", "3", "FOUR", "Five!"); ten_seconds 1387 ("Quinn, stop wasting time! Hurry up!"); time_up 1388 ("Time's up! / Time's up!")
callout countdown           1386
callout ten_seconds         1387
callout time_up             1388

